          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765313475654"
          },
          "code": "GETOPENAPIACCOUNTPRODUCT",
          "id": "1765313423915",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"OpenApiAccountProducts\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {}\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "OpenApiAccountProductTruncated",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var openApiJson = $context.$nodes.GETOPENAPIACCOUNTPRODUCT.$output;\nvar schemas = (openApiJson.components && openApiJson.components.schemas) ? openApiJson.components.schemas : {};\nvar businessObjects = [];\n\nfor (var schemaName in schemas) {\n  if (!schemas.hasOwnProperty(schemaName)) continue;\n  var schemaDef = schemas[schemaName];\n  if (!schemaDef.allOf) continue;\n\n  var boTitle = null, boDescription = null, fieldsRefName = null;\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < schemaDef.allOf.length; i++) {\n    var part = schemaDef.allOf[i];\n    if (part.type === \"object\" && (part.title || part.description)) {\n      boTitle = part.title || schemaName;\n      boDescription = part.description || \"\";\n    }\n    if (part.$ref) fieldsRefName = part.$ref.replace(\"#/components/schemas/\", \"\");\n  }\n\n  if (!boTitle || !fieldsRefName) continue;\n\n  var fieldsSchema = schemas[fieldsRefName];\n  if (!fieldsSchema || !fieldsSchema.properties) continue;\n\n  var attributes = [];\n  for (var attrName in fieldsSchema.properties) {\n    if (!fieldsSchema.properties.hasOwnProperty(attrName)) continue;\n    var attrDef = fieldsSchema.properties[attrName];\n    attributes.push({ name: attrName, description: attrDef.description || \"No description available\" });\n  }\n\n  businessObjects.push({\n    businessObjectName: schemaName,\n    businessObjectTitle: boTitle,\n    businessObjectDescription: boDescription,\n    fieldsSchemaName: fieldsRefName,\n    attributes: attributes\n  });\n}\n\nreturn businessObjects;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765313552160"
          },
          "code": "OPENAPIACCOUNTPRODUCTTRUNCATED",
          "id": "1765313475654",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "BuildExtractionQueryParameters"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765313603221"
          },
          "code": "BUILDEXTRACTIONQUERYPARAMETERS",
          "id": "1765313552160",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765313552164_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## ROLE\nYou are an AI assistant that converts natural language queries about customer accounts and products into the required SQL parameter JSON for a predefined extraction query.\n\n## INPUT SOURCES\n- Raw Account Product Data:\n  {{$context.$nodes.OPENAPIACCOUNTPRODUCTTRUNCATED.$output.result}}\n- User Query:\n {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n## EXTRACTION QUERY PARAMETERS\nThe SQL extraction uses:\n- p_filter → product-level filtering\n- p_where → aggregated account-level filtering\n- p_order_by → sorting logic\n- p_offset → OFFSET\n- p_row_count → Number of records to be fetched from offset\n\n\n\n\n\n## SECTION 1 — Allowed Fields\n### Base-level (for p_filter)\naccountProductIdentifier, accountId, accountName, registryIdentifier, accountUniqueName, currencyCode, productName, productType, productLevel, productLevel1Name, productLevel2Name, productLevel3Name, productLevel4Name, productLevel5Name, productLevel6Name, productLevel7Name, productLevel8Name, productLevel9Name, productLevel10Name, annualRecurringRevenue, investmentAmount, investmentTenure, renewalDate, engagementTrend, ownershipStatus, openPriorityOne, totalPriorityOneLastSixMonths, productFitStrength\n\n### Aggregated-level (for p_where, p_order_by)\naccountId, accountName, accountUniqueName, registryIdentifier, currencyCode, annualRecurringRevenue, renewalDate, investmentAmount, investmentTenure, engagementTrend, openPriorityOne, totalPriorityOneLastSixMonths, ownedProducts, suggestedProducts\n\n## SECTION 2 — Interpretation Rules\n- p_filter = product-level conditions\n- p_where = aggregated account-level conditions\n- p_order_by = sorting logic\n- p_row_count = derived row count\n- p_offset = always 0\n\n## SECTION 3 — SQL Construction Rules\nUse Oracle SQL.\nNever include: WHERE, ORDER BY, OFFSET, FETCH.\nAllowed:\nfield = 'VALUE'\nfield IN ('A','B')\nfield LIKE '%VALUE%'\nfield > NUMBER\nfield between NUMBER AND NUMBER\n\n### Date Handling\nInterpret relative to sysdate:\nrenewalDate between sysdate AND sysdate + 30\nrenewalDate > DATE '2026-01-01'\n\n## SECTION 4 — Semantic Mappings\ncustomer/company → accountName  \nARR → annualRecurringRevenue  \npriority 1 → openPriorityOne or totalPriorityOneLastSixMonths  \nowned products → ownershipStatus = 'ORA_ACTIVE'  \nstrong fit → productFitStrength = 'Strong'  \nexpansion products → productFitStrength = 'Strong'  \nrenewals in 30 days → renewalDate filter  \n\n## SECTION 5 — Parameter Derivation Rules\n\n### 5.0 p_row_count\nIf query says \"Top 5 ...\" → 5  \nIf missing → Use a default value of 10\n\n### 5.2 p_filter\nUse:\n- Any allowed attribute from Base-level\n\nExamples:\nannualRecurringRevenue > 15000000  \nannualRecurringRevenue between 10000000 AND 15000000  \nrenewalDate between sysdate AND sysdate + 30  \nrenewalDate > DATE '2026-01-01'  \n\nIf cannot derive or not defined by user: \"1=1\"\nUse p_filter only is user is requesting filter on individual product.\n\n### 5.2 p_where\nUse:\n- Any allowed attribute from Aggregated-level\n\nExamples:\nannualRecurringRevenue > 15000000  \nannualRecurringRevenue BETWEEN 10000000 AND 15000000  \nrenewalDate BETWEEN SYSDATE AND SYSDATE + 30  \nrenewalDate > DATE '2026-01-01'  \n\nIf cannot derive or not defined by user: \"1=1\"\nIf user is asking for filter on individual product, do not apply same filter for aggregate also\n\n### 5.3 p_order_by\nAllowed:\n- Any allowed attribute from Aggregated-level\n \n\nExamples:\nannualRecurringRevenue:desc\nrenewalDate:asc \n\nDefaults:\n- annualRecurringRevenue:desc\n-renewalDate:asc \n- cannot derive or not defined by user → \"accountName:asc\"\n\n## SECTION 6 — Default Rules\np_row_count → 10  \np_offset → 0  \np_order_by → annualRecurringRevenue:desc\np_filter → 1=1  \np_where → 1=1  \n\n## SECTION 7 — Validation Rules\n- Use only allowed fields  \n- Do not invent fields  \n- Ignore unmapped terms  \n\n## SECTION 8 — REQUIRED OUTPUT FORMAT\nAlways output ONLY JSON:\n\n{\n  \"p_filter\": \"<SQL predicate>\",\n  \"p_where\": \"<SQL predicate>\",\n  \"p_order_by\": \"<order expression>\",\n  \"p_offset\": <integer>,\n  \"p_row_count\": <integer>\n}\n\nNo explanations or comments. Only JSON."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"p_filter\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"p_where\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"p_order_by\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"p_offset\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    },\n    \"p_row_count\": {\n      \"type\": \"integer\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
